message: "If you use HyperChess Core in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "HyperChess Core"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "HyperChess Developer Team"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hyperchessdev/hyperchess-core"
url: "https://github.com/hyperchessdev/hyperchess-core"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - chess
  - chess-variant
  - game-engine
  - alpha-beta-search
  - monte-carlo-tree-search
  - webassembly
abstract: >-
  HyperChess Core is an open-source engine for HyperChess, a 12x12 chess variant with two
  jumping pieces (Eagle and Hawk). It provides bitboard move generation, an anytime
  alpha-beta search with transposition table and modern pruning/ordering heuristics, a UCT
  Monte Carlo Tree Search, a CLI/UCI/REST driver, and a TypeScript/WebAssembly SDK.
